# AI Visibility Platform — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) in the repo root:   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Fill in ANY ONE key below and run — the pipeline (providers="auto") uses every provider
# that has a key. Leave ALL of them empty to run the fully offline synthetic demo
# (clearly labelled "synthetic" in the dashboard; no network calls).
#
# Real environment variables (shell exports, Docker `environment:`) override this file.
# Keys are never logged or returned by the API. Blank values mean "not configured";
# blank *_MODEL values fall back to the defaults shown.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy. `.env`, `.env.local` and every `.env.*` except this
# file are gitignored. Only this template, with blank values, belongs in git. If a key is
# ever pushed, revoke it at the provider immediately; deleting the commit is not enough.

# --- Google Gemini --------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# --- OpenAI (or any proxy that speaks OpenAI's API, via OPENAI_BASE_URL) --------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# --- Groq (free tier available: https://console.groq.com/keys) ------------------------
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# Free tier for gpt-oss-120b: 30 requests/min, 8K tokens/min, 200K tokens/day (reasoning
# tokens count). The app caps each answer, uses low reasoning effort and paces requests
# from Groq's rate-limit headers so a run slows down instead of hitting 429s. A run is
# roughly questions x answers-per-question calls at up to ~1K tokens each, so a few
# "standard" runs a day fit the daily budget. On a paid tier you can raise these:
# GROQ_MAX_TOKENS=1024
# GROQ_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# GROQ_RPM=30

# --- OpenRouter (many models, some free: https://openrouter.ai/keys) ------------------
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# --- Anthropic Claude -----------------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# --- Ollama (local models, no key). Setting OLLAMA_BASE_URL enables it for "auto". ----
# From Docker, use http://host.docker.internal:11434
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# --- Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint (LM Studio, vLLM, Together, ...) ------------
# Needs both a base URL (ending in /v1 for most servers) and a model; key is optional.
CUSTOM_LLM_BASE_URL=
CUSTOM_LLM_API_KEY=
CUSTOM_LLM_MODEL=

# --- Storage --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where snapshots / brands / replay cache are written (default: backend/data locally;
# docker-compose pins it to /data inside the brandlens-data volume).
# DATA_DIR=

# --- Docker demo seeding (NOT read from this file) -------------------------------------
# On first start with an empty volume, the backend seeds 3 rounds of synthetic demo data.
# docker-compose substitutes SEED_DEMO from your shell, so disable seeding with:
#   SEED_DEMO=0 make up

# --- CORS (only needed once the backend is deployed somewhere other than localhost;
# see DEPLOY.md) -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exact browser origins allowed to call this API, comma-separated. Not needed for
# localhost dev (Vite :5173, docker-compose's nginx :8080 are always allowed).
#   CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app
# Optional: a regex for origins that vary, e.g. Vercel's per-PR preview deploys.
#   CORS_ORIGIN_REGEX=https://.*\.vercel\.app
